1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,207
A taxonomy holds the terms you sort content with.

2
00:00:04,207 --> 00:00:08,931
A Taxonomy Field attaches them to a content type, so editors can pick them.

3
00:00:08,931 --> 00:00:13,071
In this video, you add Category and Tags fields to Blog Post, use

4
00:00:13,071 --> 00:00:15,520
both, and see the terms on the site.

5
00:00:20,120 --> 00:00:25,552
A taxonomy is a managed vocabulary, and this site has two, Categories and Tags.

6
00:00:25,552 --> 00:00:29,641
It is made of terms, and terms can sit inside other terms.

7
00:00:29,641 --> 00:00:33,348
A Taxonomy Field lets a content type use a taxonomy:

8
00:00:33,348 --> 00:00:35,840
you attach the field to the type.

9
00:00:36,590 --> 00:00:41,507
Editors pick terms while they edit an item, and the field offers two editors.

10
00:00:41,507 --> 00:00:45,950
The Standard editor shows every term as a checkbox or a radio button.

11
00:00:45,950 --> 00:00:49,741
The Tags editor is a box where you type to search, and can

12
00:00:49,741 --> 00:00:51,400
create tags as you go.

13
00:00:52,150 --> 00:00:57,745
Each field uses one taxonomy, and its settings define the rules for the selection:

14
00:00:57,745 --> 00:01:00,225
Required, Unique and Leaves only.

15
00:01:00,225 --> 00:01:05,947
The display mode, Standard or Tags, decides how the chosen terms appear on the page.

16
00:01:05,947 --> 00:01:09,380
Let's build one field of each kind on Blog Post.

17
00:01:13,567 --> 00:01:18,144
Content types are under Design, Content Definition, Content Types.

18
00:01:18,144 --> 00:01:23,547
Let's edit Blog Post, which has two fields here, a Subtitle and a Banner Image.

19
00:01:24,004 --> 00:01:25,773
Add Field opens a form.

20
00:01:25,773 --> 00:01:29,861
The Display Name is what editors see, so let's type Category.

21
00:01:29,861 --> 00:01:32,424
The Technical Name fills in from it.

22
00:01:32,874 --> 00:01:35,367
Field Type lists the kinds of field.

23
00:01:35,367 --> 00:01:40,293
Let's choose Taxonomy Field, and then Save & Configure, which saves the field

24
00:01:40,293 --> 00:01:42,014
and opens its settings.

25
00:01:42,471 --> 00:01:47,920
Taxonomy is where the field draws its terms from, and Categories is the one to select.

26
00:01:47,920 --> 00:01:51,770
The Hint is a line of help that editors see with the field,

27
00:01:51,770 --> 00:01:53,251
so let's write one.

28
00:01:53,709 --> 00:01:57,656
Required makes a selection mandatory, and it stays off here.

29
00:01:57,656 --> 00:02:02,441
Unique allows one term only, and Leaves only restricts the choice to terms

30
00:02:02,441 --> 00:02:04,474
with no children below them.

31
00:02:04,474 --> 00:02:05,969
Let's turn on both.

32
00:02:06,430 --> 00:02:08,057
Below are two questions:

33
00:02:08,057 --> 00:02:10,282
What type of editor should be used?

34
00:02:10,282 --> 00:02:12,832
What type of display mode should be used?

35
00:02:12,832 --> 00:02:15,980
Both stay on Standard, and Save stores the settings.

36
00:02:16,468 --> 00:02:21,554
Back on Blog Post, Category is listed as a Taxonomy Field, below the

37
00:02:21,554 --> 00:02:24,028
Subtitle and the Banner Image.

38
00:02:28,253 --> 00:02:32,090
Back on Blog Post, the Tags field starts the same way:

39
00:02:32,090 --> 00:02:37,973
Add Field, the Display Name Tags, the field type Taxonomy Field, and Save & Configure.

40
00:02:38,442 --> 00:02:42,953
This time the Taxonomy is Tags, and Required, Unique and Leaves only stay

41
00:02:42,953 --> 00:02:45,751
off, so a post can have any number of tags.

42
00:02:45,751 --> 00:02:50,205
Placeholder replaces the text Type to search in the Tags editor, and the

43
00:02:50,205 --> 00:02:52,090
Standard editor ignores it.

44
00:02:52,090 --> 00:02:53,632
Let's leave it empty.

45
00:02:54,091 --> 00:02:57,098
Next, let's set the editor question to Tags.

46
00:02:57,098 --> 00:03:02,631
One more setting appears, called Open, which lets editors create tags while they type.

47
00:03:03,083 --> 00:03:07,705
The hint of Open notes that a tag created this way has only its display text.

48
00:03:07,705 --> 00:03:09,153
Let's leave Open on.

49
00:03:09,622 --> 00:03:14,106
Let's also set the display mode question to Tags, so the page displays

50
00:03:14,106 --> 00:03:15,522
the field as tags.

51
00:03:15,522 --> 00:03:17,352
Save stores the settings.

52
00:03:17,934 --> 00:03:22,506
Tags is listed with two badges, one for its display mode and one

53
00:03:22,506 --> 00:03:25,119
for its editor, both reading Tags.

54
00:03:25,119 --> 00:03:28,974
Category has none, because it uses the Standard ones.

55
00:03:33,274 --> 00:03:35,981
This list of posts comes from the Blog menu.

56
00:03:35,981 --> 00:03:39,934
Edit opens the post A Night Train Across the Alps, and its Category

57
00:03:39,934 --> 00:03:42,534
and Tags fields are further down the page.

58
00:03:43,003 --> 00:03:47,743
Category shows its Hint, then the terms of the Categories taxonomy as radio

59
00:03:47,743 --> 00:03:49,849
buttons, because Unique is on.

60
00:03:49,849 --> 00:03:52,073
Trains is indented under Travel.

61
00:03:52,530 --> 00:03:58,267
Travel is disabled, because Leaves only restricts the choice to terms with no children.

62
00:03:58,267 --> 00:03:59,870
Let's select Trains.

63
00:04:00,377 --> 00:04:03,405
Tags is a box with the placeholder Type to search.

64
00:04:03,405 --> 00:04:07,677
Let's type the first letters of Exploration, and select it from the list.

65
00:04:08,167 --> 00:04:11,521
To create a tag, type a name that is not in the list.

66
00:04:11,521 --> 00:04:15,897
Let's type Night Train, and the box offers Press enter to create a tag.

67
00:04:16,437 --> 00:04:21,649
Pressing Enter adds Night Train to the Tags taxonomy right away, and selects it.

68
00:04:21,649 --> 00:04:26,497
Only users with the Manage taxonomies permission can create tags this way.

69
00:04:26,986 --> 00:04:30,996
Publish saves the post with its category and its two tags.

70
00:04:35,296 --> 00:04:38,916
Back in the Blog list, View opens the post on the site.

71
00:04:41,302 --> 00:04:45,327
Below the text, the category shows as a badge, and each tag as

72
00:04:45,327 --> 00:04:46,807
a badge of its own.

73
00:04:46,807 --> 00:04:51,602
The field stores the choice, and the theme's templates decide how it looks.

74
00:04:53,602 --> 00:04:57,638
A Taxonomy Field attaches the terms of one taxonomy to a content type:

75
00:04:57,638 --> 00:05:01,834
the Standard editor shows every term, and the Tags editor lets you search

76
00:05:01,834 --> 00:05:03,481
for tags and create them.

77
00:05:03,481 --> 00:05:04,862
Thanks for watching.

